{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After escalation, an unavailable second implementer can cause the run to repeat work on an already exhausted model."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An environment-blocked verification can retry the same model and stop without the intended reassessment by an available alternative."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The warning misidentifies the previous verifier as the implementer when explaining why a pinned retry reused a model."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A pinned decision chain discards an otherwise usable last-resort answer and requests human intervention."},{"id":"C3b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The warning attributes a finder-vendor match to the implementer, misleading the operator about the overridden preference."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A completed review can claim no other vendor was available even when pinned routing selected among available alternatives."}]}